sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/wolfram2002-ch03-20> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The four themes of repetition, nesting, randomness and localized structures are the dominant types of behavior across a vast range of systems, and these overall behavior types are almost independent of the details of the underlying rules.";
    dc:type "general-principle";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Repetition, nesting, randomness and localized structures dominate everywhere";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Stephen Wolfram, A New Kind of Science (Champaign, IL: Wolfram Media, 2002), Chapter 3, “The World of Simple Programs”; section “Some Conclusions” (from p. 105), p. 106. Scope: simple programs and, by extension, a vast range of systems"
}
